    <string name="why_it_works">why it is built this way</string>
    <string name="why_it_works_text">Writing a count down, and telling someone, makes a goal hold better (138 experiments). A streak motivates, but a broken streak shown as a loss makes people give up, and after a slip it is the lost confidence, not the guilt, that leads to relapse: so a slip costs one day and the totals stay. Each urge beaten is proof you can. An urge peaks and passes, and keeping the mind busy for a few minutes lowers it. A plan decided in advance roughly doubles the odds of following it. A start on a Monday or a first of the month carries further. The sources are in the app\'s repository.</string>
